            <div xml:id="d596">

                <pb facs="0526" n="410" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg410"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 822.032/9.]</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The American Chargé d’Affaires to the Secretary of
                        State</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 130.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Quinto</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1912-08-12">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">August 12, 1912</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to report that on
                    Saturday, August 10, the Ecuadorian Congress assembled in regular session for
                    the year 1912. Dr. Alfredo Baquerizo Moreno was elected President of the Senate
                    and according to the Constitution will be acting President until September
                    first, 1912, when General Plaza will assume the office.</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Rutherford Bingham</hi>.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
